From 6df68b15d6bf5500e30ada590498319c48c170b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hardening <hardening@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:27:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] build: drop Xvfb/mesa/llvm, vim and Node headers (2.87 ->
 2.58 GB)

Everything here is dead weight for a headless-only image:

- Xvfb + mesa (libgl1-mesa-dri -> libLLVM-15, 112 MB, plus 25 MB of dri drivers)
  are installed by `playwright install --with-deps` for headed rendering. ARTEX
  launches @playwright/mcp with --headless and the headless shell renders through
  its bundled SwiftShader. Verified after removal: screenshot of a rendered page
  and a live WebGL context both still work, as uid 10001 -> 173 MB.
- vim + vim-runtime: 43 MB, no skill invokes it (grep over skills/ is empty; the
  agents use cat/sed/python).
- Node headers copied along with the Node binary from the build stage: 7 MB.

Not touched, because they are functional rather than leftover: /opt/bbot 508 MB,
/ms-playwright 288 MB, the six Go recon tools ~436 MB (already stripped, nuclei
alone is 177 MB), Node 124 MB, Python 3.12. Going lower means giving up a
capability (see HARDENING.md for the three options).

Verified: compose stack healthy, GET / -> 200, bbot dry-run 14/14 modules as
uid 10001, nmap/git/nuclei still present.
---
 Dockerfile   | 11 +++++++++--
 HARDENING.md | 17 +++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
index e921215..0b01bbe 100644
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ ARG TARGETARCH
 COPY --from=web /usr/local /usr/local
 
 RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
-      ca-certificates ripgrep curl wget vim git jq unzip \
+      ca-certificates ripgrep curl wget git jq unzip \
       dnsutils iputils-ping netcat-openbsd inetutils-telnet whois nmap \
       p7zip-full xz-utils \
     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
@@ -214,7 +214,14 @@ RUN npm install -g --no-fund --no-audit \
     # headless Chromium runs the chromium-headless-shell build, so the ~420 MB headed
     # Chromium never starts. Drop it; ffmpeg stays (screenshots/video need it).
     && playwright install --with-deps --only-shell chromium \
-    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* /root/.npm /root/.cache/node
+    # --with-deps also pulls Xvfb and mesa for headed rendering: libgl1-mesa-dri
+    # drags in libLLVM-15 (112 MB) plus 25 MB of dri drivers. Headless Chromium
+    # renders through the bundled SwiftShader instead; verified that screenshots and
+    # a WebGL context still work with all of it removed (~170 MB).
+    && apt-get purge -y -qq xvfb libgl1-mesa-dri libglx-mesa0 libgl1 libglx0 \
+    && apt-get autoremove -y -qq --purge \
+    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* /var/cache/apt \
+              /root/.npm /root/.cache/node /usr/local/include/node
 
 WORKDIR /app
 # Binary compiled from source in the build stage above.
diff --git a/HARDENING.md b/HARDENING.md
index 9e9e601..3810de8 100644
--- a/HARDENING.md
+++ b/HARDENING.md
@@ -114,7 +114,16 @@ offering them the corresponding source of the modified version.
 > 127.0.0.1:8787, bbot 3.0.2 running as uid 10001). Re-verify after changing any version
 > pin: `docker build --progress=plain -t artex:local .`
 >
-> Size: 6.49 GB → 2.87 GB (`docker system df -v`). Removed: 1.5 GB of bbot build junk in
-> `/root` (tool cache + gcc/make/libssl-dev/ansible installs), 92 MB pip cache, 55 MB npm
-> cache, and the 422 MB headed Chromium that `--headless` never starts. `/usr` also drops
-> from 1.70 GB to 1.12 GB now that bbot's build tooling stays in the `bbotdeps` stage.
+> Size: 6.49 GB → 2.58 GB (`docker system df -v`; 1.83 GB measured with `du`). Removed:
+> 1.5 GB of bbot build junk in `/root` (tool cache + gcc/make/libssl-dev/ansible installs),
+> 92 MB pip cache, 55 MB npm cache, the 422 MB headed Chromium that `--headless` never
+> starts, 173 MB of Xvfb/mesa/libLLVM-15 that `--with-deps` installs for headed rendering
+> (headless Chromium uses the bundled SwiftShader; screenshots and WebGL verified after
+> removal), ~43 MB of `vim` + vim-runtime (no skill invokes it), and 7 MB of Node headers.
+>
+> What is left is mostly functional: `/opt/bbot` 508 MB (of which 234 MB is the unpinned
+> module deps above), `/ms-playwright` 288 MB (headless shell + ffmpeg), the six Go tools
+> in `/usr/local/bin` ~436 MB (already stripped; nuclei alone is 177 MB), Node 124 MB and
+> Python 3.12. The three ways to go lower are capability trades, not cleanup: install bbot
+> module deps only for the modules the skill uses (-234 MB, breaks ad-hoc modules), drop
+> bbot (-508 MB), or drop the browser MCP (-412 MB for Playwright + Node).
